id=a52sxq_gallery_slowmo
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: hold a video in Gallery to play it in slow motion
author=kusti420
description=Samsung Gallery's Instant Slow-mo (hold a playing video) is gated on SEC_FLOATING_FEATURE_CAMERA_SUPPORT_AIFRC and plays through SemMediaPlayer.setVideoFrc() -> libaplayer -> the vendor MPP HAL's AI frame rate conversion pipe (libmppaifrc + SNPE 2.x models). The A52s vendor (MPP HAL V1, SNPE 1.x) has no such pipe and the S26 Ultra one cannot run on it (its models ship without weights and are compiled for the newer DSP), so the feature is stripped. This patch brings the gesture back without touching the Gallery APK (it stays Samsung-signed and Galaxy Store updatable). Framework side: inside the Gallery process only, SemFloatingFeature reports the feature and its limits, and SemMediaPlayer.setVideoFrc() goes through K4SlowMo. Native side: libaplayer's Instant Slow-mo path is pointed at the A52s vendor's own classic frame rate conversion pipe (MPP type 3, OpenCL motion interpolation, exact x2), fed with byte buffers because the V1 HAL has no input surface call; libimageconverter learns the pipe's NV12 output format. K4SlowMo picks one of three paths per hold. Neural: when the k4front MPP store of the gallery_slowmo_neural patch (the k4neuralmpp daemon) is registered and persist.sys.k4.slowmo_neural is not 0 (default 1), eligible sources (8-bit SDR, up to 1920x1088 at 30 fps for now) are requested at x4 and play at a true 0.25x with three generated frames per real one; opening such a video in Gallery sends the daemon a one-way warm-up so its network is ready by the first hold. Classical: otherwise 8-bit SDR sources up to 1920x1088 at 30 fps play at 0.5x with every second frame interpolated (about 30 shown frames per second instead of 15); persist.sys.k4.slowmo_frc=2 selects Gallery's own 0.25x through the pipe (15 per second instead of 7.5), =0 switches the pipe off. Plain: everything the pipes cannot take (10-bit/HDR, above 1080p, above 30 fps, streams) and every refusal by the native player falls back to plain playback at 0.25x as before. Logcat tag K4SlowMo says per hold which path ran and why the better ones were skipped. Costs: the picture freezes for a little under a second when the hold starts (the player rebuilds its video path, as on the S26 Ultra), and after the first hold the video keeps running through the pipe in pass-through until it is closed. The real floating_feature.xml is unchanged, so Camera, MotionPhoto, Video Player, the share sheet and libaplayer's other AI FRC users (motion photo dynamic viewing, temporal zoom) keep their non-AIFRC paths. Gallery's other entry points behind the same flag: "Save slow-mo clip" exports through VEKit, which falls back to a plain re-timed clip when its AI FRC pipe is missing (0.25x, every frame repeated four times, audio kept; SDR and HDR10 checked on 9.3.15); the motion photo view modes "Boomerang" and "Slow-mo" need libaplayer's dynamic viewing, which the native player drops without AI FRC, so they are switched off again from the framework side (MotionPhotoViewMode.mEnabled, by reflection on Gallery's main thread) and the spinner offers "Motion photo" and "Off" as on any phone without AI FRC.
